# The tb-updater test library inspects the dpkg database on purpose, to assert the
# real package state the suite is validating.
dist-ai: uses-dpkg-database-directly
# Each suite ships its README / THREAT-MODEL next to its tests under
# usr/share/<suite>-tests/, documenting the directory it sits in -- the case lintian
# itself says to override. Context-less: it holds for all ~44 suites, and a per-file
# list would drift as suites are added or removed.
dist-ai: package-contains-documentation-outside-usr-share-doc
# evil.example (RFC 2606 reserved) is a FAKE cross-origin host used ONLY as test-fixture
# input in the jscov suite -- the book-nav tests feed it to the handler to PROVE it
# REFUSES to navigate cross-origin (navSafe same-origin gate; no Referer/onion leak). It
# is test data in a JS string, never a resource any shipped page loads. privacy-breach-generic
# skips the standard rel=next/prev but flags the custom rel=mw-book-next carrier, so the
# fixture trips it; the host name scopes the override to the fake test domain only.
dist-ai: privacy-breach-generic *evil.example*
